#: global.cpp:409
#, kde-format
msgid "Free Crossword"
msgstr "Slobodna križaljka"

#: global.cpp:411
#, kde-format
msgctxt "Short description of the crossword type 'Free'"
msgid "This is a special type that tries to be least restrictive."
msgstr "Ovo je poseban tip koji pokušava da bude najmanje ograničen."

#: global.cpp:413
#, kde-format
msgctxt "Long description of the crossword type 'Free'"
msgid ""
"This is a special type that tries to be least restrictive. You can use all "
"available cell types (eg. clue cells, double clue cells, image cells, "
"solution letter cells). You can mix answers that have a clue cell with "
"answers that don't. Answers may contain characters as well as numbers."
msgstr ""
"Ovo je poseban tip koji pokušava da bude najmanje ograničen. Možete "
"koristiti sve dostupne tipove ćelija (pr. ćelije traga, duple ćelije traga, "
"ćelije slike, ćelije slova rješenja). Možete mješati odgovore koji imaju "
"ćeliju traga sa odgovorima koji nemaju. Odgovori mogu sadržavati znakove, "
"kao i brojeve."

#: global.cpp:424
#, kde-format
msgid "User Defined Crossword"
msgstr "Korisnički definirana križaljka"

#: global.cpp:426
#, kde-format
msgctxt "Short description of the crossword type 'User Defined'"
msgid "Lets you specify your own rules."
msgstr "Dopušta da definišete vlastita pravila."

#: global.cpp:434
#, kde-format
msgid "Swedish Crossword"
msgstr "Švedska križaljka"

#: global.cpp:436
#, kde-format
msgctxt "Short description of the crossword type 'Swedish'"
msgid ""
"Swedish crosswords contain clue cells which contain the clue text in it and "
"an arrow to indicate in which direction the clues have to be answered."
msgstr ""
"Švedske križaljke sadrže ćelije traga koje sadrže tekst traga u sebi i "
"strelicu koja pokazuje u kojem pravcu tragovi moraju biti odgovoreni."

#: global.cpp:439
#, kde-format
msgctxt "Long description of the crossword type 'Swedish'"
msgid ""
"The \"Swedish-Style\" grid uses no clue numbers - the clues are contained in "
"the cells which would normally be black in other countries. Arrows indicate "
"in which direction the clues have to be answered, vertical or horizontal. "
"This style of grid is used in several countries other than Sweden, usually "
"in magazines with pages of A4 or similar size. The grid often has a photo of "
"a pop or movie star replacing a block of squares, as a clue to one answer. "
"These puzzles usually have no symmetry in the grid.\n"
"Crosswords with clue cells inside the crossword grid are also called "
"\"Arrowwords\", \"Pointers\" or \"Tipwords\" in English, \"Autodefinidos\" "
"in Spanish, \"Mots Fléchés\" in French, etc.\n"
"(text taken from wikipedia)"
msgstr ""
"Skandinavka ne koristi brojeve u opisima - opisi se nalaze u ćeliji koja bi "
"normalno bila crna u drugim državama. Strelice naznačavaju u kojem smjeru su "
"tragovi koji moraju biti odgovoreni, vertikalno ili horizontalno. Stil same "
"rešetke je korišten u više država,a ne samo u Švedskoj, obično u magazinima "
"sa stranicama formata A4 ili sličnim veličinama.  Rešetka često ima sliku "
"ili filmsku zvijezdu koja zamjenjuje određeni blok kockica, kao trag za "
"jedno rješejne. Ove zagonetke obično nemaju simetriju u rešteci.\n"
"Križaljke sa ćelijaama koje predstavljaju tragove se još nazivaju i "
"\"Arrowwords\", \"Pointers\" ili \"TipWords\" na Engleskom, \"Autodefinidos"
"\" na španskom, \"Mots Fleches\" na Francuskom, itd."

#: global.cpp:457
#, kde-format
msgid "American Crossword"
msgstr "Američka križaljka"

#: global.cpp:459
#, kde-format
msgctxt "Short description of the crossword type 'American'"
msgid ""
"American crosswords have numbered clues and a list of clues on the side of "
"the crossword. They have usually 180 degree rotational symmetry."
msgstr ""
"Američka križaljka ima numeričke tragove i listu tragova sa strane "
"križaljke. One obično imaju 180 stepeni racionalnu simetriju."

#: global.cpp:462
#, kde-format
msgctxt "Long description of the crossword type 'American'"
msgid ""
"Crossword grids such as those appearing in most North American newspapers "
"and magazines feature solid areas of white squares. Every letter is checked, "
"and usually each answer is required to contain at least three letters. In "
"such puzzles shaded squares are traditionally limited to about one-sixth of "
"the design. Crossword grids elsewhere, such as in Britain and Australia, "
"have a lattice-like structure, with a higher percentage of shaded squares, "
"leaving up to half the letters in an answer unchecked. For example, if the "
"top row has an answer running all the way across, there will be no across "
"answers in the second row.\n"
"Another tradition in puzzle design (in North America and Britain "
"particularly) is that the grid should have 180-degree rotational symmetry, "
"so that its pattern appears the same if the paper is turned upside down. "
"Most puzzle designs also require that all white cells be orthogonally "
"contiguous (that is, connected in one mass through shared sides, to form a "
"single polyomino).\n"
"(text taken from wikipedia)"
msgstr ""
"Rešetke križaljki kao onih što se najčešće pojavljuju u novinama i "
"magazinima u Sjevernoj Americi su nepromjenjive površine sa bijelim "
"kvadratima. Svako slovo je provjereno, i obično za svaki odgovor se "
"podrazumjeva da sadrži bar tri karaktera. Rešetke križaljki bilo gdje drugo,"
"kao npr u Velikoj Britaniji i Australiji, imaju rešetkastu strukturu, sa "
"velikim procentom zatamljenih kvadrata, ostavljajući pola karaktera u "
"odgvorou neprovjerenim. Npr. ukoliko se trenutno odgovor unosi u prvi red, "
"tada se odgovori neće prikazivati u drugom redu.\n"
"Slijedeća tradicija u dizajnu križaljki ( u Sjevernoj Americi i Britaniji ) "
"je da rešetka bi trebala imat rotacijsku simetriju takvu da se patern "
"prikaže korektno i ukoliko je papir okrenut naopako. Većina dizajna "
"zagonetki također zahtjevaju da sve bijle ćelije imaju ortogonalnu "
"neprekidnost."

#: global.cpp:488
#, kde-format
msgid "Number Puzzle"
msgstr "Numerička zagonetka"

#: global.cpp:490
#, kde-format
msgctxt "Short description of the crossword type 'Number Puzzle'"
msgid ""
"Number puzzles are a variant of crosswords in which each cell has a number "
"between 1 and 26. The solver has to find out for which letter of the "
"alphabet a number stands."
msgstr ""
"Numeričke zagonetke su varijante križaljki u kojima svaka ćelija ima broj "
"između 1 i 26. Rješavač mora saznati za koje slovo abecede važi koji broj."

#: global.cpp:503
#, kde-format
msgid "Crossnumber"
msgstr "Ukršteni brojevi"

#: global.cpp:505
#, kde-format
msgctxt "Short description of the crossword type 'Crossnumber'"
msgid ""
"Crossnumbers are the numerical analogy of a crossword, in which the "
"solutions to the clues are numbers instead of words."
msgstr ""
"Crossnumber-i su numerička analogija križaljke, u kojima su rješenja tragova "
"brojevi umjesto riječi."

#: global.cpp:508
#, kde-format
msgctxt "Long description of the crossword type 'Crossnumber'"
msgid ""
"A crossnumber (also known as a cross-figure) is the numerical analogy of a "
"crossword, in which the solutions to the clues are numbers instead of words. "
"Clues are usually arithmetical expressions, but can also be general "
"knowledge clues to which the answer is a number or year. There are also "
"numerical fill-in crosswords.\n"
"The Daily Mail Weekend magazine used to feature crossnumbers under the "
"misnomer Number Word. This kind of puzzle should not be confused with a "
"different puzzle that the Daily Mail refers to as Cross Number.\n"
"(text taken from wikipedia)"
msgstr ""
"Ukršteni bojevi (takođe poznat kao unakrsnom figura) je brojčana analogija "
"jedne križaljke, u kojem su rešenja za tragovima su brojevi umesto reči. "
"Tragovi su obično aritmetičke izrazi, ali takođe može biti tragovi opšteg "
"znanja na koje je odgovor broj ili godinua Postoje i numerička "
"dosvetljavanje ukrštenih reči.\n"
"he Daily Mail Weekend časopis nekada ukrštene brojeve pod pogrešno naziva "
"Number Word. Ovu vrstu zagonetke ne treba miješati sa drugom iz Daily "
"Mailgdje se zove Cross Number\n"
"(Tekst preuzet sa vikipedije)"

